    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "23 Laurel Park presents an excellent opportunity to acquire a generously proportioned four-bedroom home, positioned on a desirable corner plot within this quiet and established residential development.\n\nThe accommodation comprises an entrance hallway, a versatile office/fourth bedroom to the right, created through the conversion of the former garage, and a comfortable living room to the front. To the rear, the kitchen/dining room enjoys direct access to the garden. Upstairs, there are two double bedrooms, one single bedroom and a family bathroom. \n\nThe property benefits from oil-fired central heating and a C-rated BER.\n\nOutside, the corner position provides ample garden space to both the front and rear, offering excellent potential for landscaping and outdoor living. \n\nLaurel Park is a mature and conveniently located development within walking distance of local schools and shops, while Carlow Town bus services and key commuter routes are also close at hand.\n\nHaving previously been rented, the property is ready for some updating and redecoration throughout. \n\nHowever, its spacious accommodation, substantial corner plot and sought-after location provide a superb opportunity for buyers wishing to modernise a home to their own taste. Viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the space and potential on offer contact us today to arrange your appointment."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Notice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> 4 bedroom configuration - one on the ground floor </li><li> Generous room proportions throughout </li><li> Large open plan kitchen / dining room </li><li> Side entrance to the rear garden - block boundary </li><li> C BER rating - oil central heating </li><li> Walking distance of local schools, shops etc </li><li> Close to commuting routes & local town bus link stop </li><li> Very quiet, well established development - facing a green area</li></ul>"
      },
